@* Shared using directives for every ZenithUI component. _Imports.razor files are additive down
   the directory tree, so each component folder inherits these and only has to declare its
   @namespace.

   Note there is no @namespace here. Each component file declares `@namespace ZenithUI` itself,
   which flattens the library into one namespace so consumers need a single @using. Putting that
   directive in an _Imports.razor instead does not scale: Razor generates a class per
   _Imports.razor, so a second folder declaring it produces a duplicate `ZenithUI._Imports` and the
   build fails with CS0111. Leaving this file without one gives it the unique
   `ZenithUI.Components` namespace. *@

@using System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis
@using System.Globalization
@using System.Linq.Expressions
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Forms
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Routing
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web
@using Microsoft.JSInterop
@using ZenithUI

@* Deliberately absent: @rendermode. A component library must never pick a render mode for the
   host application - the consumer decides whether a page is static, Server or WebAssembly. *@
